          "title": "You'll want to know: 打开",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "打开 — dǎkāi — \"to open; to switch on\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "你去打开书房的门 nǐ qù dǎkāi shūfáng de mén — Go and open the study door."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "打开 (dǎkāi) is built from 打 'to strike' and 开 'to open', both inherited from Middle Chinese, taengX and khoj (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), though dǎ is not the sound taengX would regularly give."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
